WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:03.229
Danger, Will Robinson...your final season
is approaching.

00:00:03.229 --> 00:00:04.390
"That was a joke."

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:07.820
"Yeah, no, I know."

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.550
Netflix has announced that Lost in Space,
the modern re-imagining of the classic '60s

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:15.360
TV series, will come to an end after its upcoming
third season.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.520
The final go-round is expected to hit the
streamer sometime in 2021.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.110
"Well, that's too bad."

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:27.150
The sci-fi revival got off to a bit of a rough
start when it debuted in April of 2018.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.380
Critics generally agreed that it looked gorgeous
and was well-acted by its formidable cast.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.640
The first season, however, was taken to task
in some quarters for not having the narrative

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.200
ambition to match its impressive visuals.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.880
"What happened?"

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.469
"There was an accident."

00:00:43.469 --> 00:00:48.040
The second season, debuting in December 2019,
was received much more warmly.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.390
Critics appreciated the added dramatic heft
that batch of episodes brought to the story

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:56.829
of the marooned Robinson family, and the special
effects were even more stunning and elaborate

00:00:56.829 --> 00:00:58.270
than in the first outing.

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:02.539
Viewers ready for some binge-watching over
the holiday season also flocked to the series,

00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:04.830
making a third season all but inevitable.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:09.340
So it was somewhat unexpected that Season
3 would actually be the series' last.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:13.220
Fortunately for the show's fans, however,
this wasn't really an unexpected development.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:18.009
According to producer and showrunner Zack
Estrin, Netflix didn't exactly pull the plug

00:01:18.009 --> 00:01:22.329
on Lost in Space; the streamer simply followed
the plan which Estrin and crew had had all

00:01:22.329 --> 00:01:23.329
along.

00:01:23.329 --> 00:01:24.329
"Cool."

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:25.329
"No.

00:01:25.329 --> 00:01:26.539
Not cool."

00:01:26.539 --> 00:01:31.770
In a statement following Netflix's announcement,
Estrin indicated that he had always had a

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:35.829
clear picture in his head of where the Robinson
family's adventures would take them, and how

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:37.909
their story would eventually conclude.

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:38.929
The statement explained,

00:01:38.929 --> 00:01:43.270
"From the beginning, we've always viewed this
particular story of the Robinsons as a trilogy,

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:47.679
a three-part epic family adventure with a
clear beginning, middle, and end.

00:01:47.679 --> 00:01:51.270
It's also worth noting that, with what these
characters go through just trying to survive

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:55.759
each episode, if anyone deserves to catch
their breath before their next mission, it's

00:01:55.759 --> 00:02:00.880
Will, Penny, Judy, Maureen, John, Don West,
Dr. Smith...and The Robot.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:02.950
And, of course, Debbie the Chicken.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:07.119
So while this chapter of Lost In Space is
coming to a rousing conclusion, I'm excited

00:02:07.119 --> 00:02:11.200
about continuing to explore new stories with
my friends at Netflix, and for all of the

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.290
incredible possibilities that lie ahead."

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:17.510
While it may be a bit disappointing for fans
that Lost in Space will be coming to a close

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:21.030
just as it appears to be picking up a head
of steam, there's definitely something to

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:24.969
be said for the series' creative team having
such a strong vision for its narrative.

00:02:24.969 --> 00:02:29.780
Sure, with such a potentially open-ended premise,
a show like Lost in Space could potentially

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:34.879
go on for season after season, but more often
than not, this is a recipe for even the most

00:02:34.879 --> 00:02:36.650
well-received shows to wear out their welcome.

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:40.980
Fans can at least be reasonably assured that
Estrin and company will end the series on

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:45.019
a high note, and that the Robinson family
will find closure in the final chapters of

00:02:45.019 --> 00:02:46.040
their story.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.349
Estrin may not exactly be a household name,
but he has a pretty sterling record as a television

00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:51.750
producer and writer.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:55.870
He cut his teeth on the series Charmed and
Dawson's Creek, and was also an executive

00:02:55.870 --> 00:03:00.609
producer on Prison Break, which ran for 5
seasons beginning in 2005.

00:03:00.609 --> 00:03:04.819
Since then, Estrin has taken on a producing
role on a number of genre series, including

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:09.260
ABC's The River, Zero Hour, and Once Upon
a Time in Wonderland.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:13.030
Netflix was satisfied enough with the performance
of Lost in Space that, in conjunction with

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:17.349
the announcement of the series' discontinuation,
it was also revealed that Estrin has signed

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:21.349
an multi-year overall deal to develop and
produce new content for the streamer.

00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:26.150
So, while fans of Lost in Space may be lamenting
the series' end, there are a couple of pretty

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:30.269
awesome takeaways here: first, that the series
will receive a planned, epic conclusion; and

00:03:30.269 --> 00:03:34.879
second, that its driving creative force will
be back with more serialized goodness in the

00:03:34.879 --> 00:03:35.879
very near future.

00:03:35.879 --> 00:03:39.829
Of course, we'll be keeping an eye out for
Estrin's upcoming projects to hit the Netflix

00:03:39.829 --> 00:03:43.030
pipeline, and we'll be sure to keep you informed.

